  "tagline": "An Apache-licensed, Postgres-compatible streaming database that stores state on S3 and writes Iceberg.",
  "description": "RisingWave is a distributed SQL streaming database: you define sources (Kafka, Pulsar, Kinesis, Postgres/MySQL CDC), materialized views and sinks in Postgres-flavoured SQL, and it maintains results incrementally. State lives in its Hummock LSM store on object storage, which makes recovery fast and compute elastic, and it can serve queries directly or sink to Iceberg, ClickHouse and other systems. Licensed Apache 2.0 with a managed cloud from RisingWave Labs, it is a common open-source alternative to Flink SQL for teams who want streaming without writing JVM jobs.",
